# Emergency braking (docs/emergency_stop.md) on the burn-in axis (10 mm a
# revolution): at 188 rad/s (300 mm/s) something fails; hv0.sim_dist,
# zeroed then, is how far the axis went (1 rad = 1.59 mm). Coasting takes
# ~16 rad (26 mm) and ~180 ms.
# The HV board's rating (conf0.max_hv_power -> qstop0.max_power): a quick
# stop feeds the braking power back into the DC bus, j * a * v; it is held
# to the rating, so at speed the deceleration is lower. Here 30 W (the
# template's 1000 W is never reached by this small motor: ~140 W at most):
# ~4.4 rad (7 mm) instead of ~2 rad. The phase current stays under
# max_ac_cur (10 A) throughout.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 300
run 1
hv0.sim_vel
hv0.sim_dist = 0
qstop0.max_power = 30
lcncstop
@sample qstop0.power 0.001 0.05
@sample hv0.abs_cur 0.001 0.05
run 0.25
hv0.sim_dist
hv0.sim_vel
@expect max qstop0.power < 30.5
@expect max qstop0.power > 25
@expect max|hv0.abs_cur| < 10
@expect hv0.sim_dist ~ 4.4 0.6
@expect hv0.sim_vel[2] ~ 0 0.5
